# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Series Hub environment
#
# OPTIONAL — live "worldwide trending" shelves with real posters, metadata and
# official trailers (YouTube embeds). Uses the TMDB API (free tier is fine):
#   1. Create an account at https://www.themoviedb.org/signup
#   2. Request an API key (Developer) at https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api
#   3. Copy this file to `.env.local` and paste your key below
#   4. Restart `npm run dev`
#
# This product uses the TMDB API but is not endorsed or certified by TMDB.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_TMDB_API_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — Supabase: sign-in (Google / GitHub / email magic link) + cloud
# sync of My List, likes, reminders and Continue-Watching progress.
#   1. Create a free project at https://supabase.com/dashboard
#   2. Authentication → Providers → enable Google (or any other)
#      (Google needs OAuth client credentials from Google Cloud Console —
#       Supabase docs walk you through it; Site URL = your app's origin)
#   3. SQL Editor → run the contents of supabase/schema.sql from this repo
#   4. Settings → API → copy the Project URL and anon public key below
# Without these, Series Hub runs in guest mode (everything stays local).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — your own licensed streaming API. GET endpoint returning JSON:
#   [ { "name": "Channel 4", "url": "https://cdn.you.com/master.m3u8",
#       "cat": "Movies", "showId": "neon-district" } ]      (or {"channels":[...]})
# URLs must be DIRECT media (.m3u8/.mpd/.mp4/.webm) you own or are licensed to
# stream — embed/iframe providers are rejected. Channels appear on the Network
# Status screen with green/yellow/red health lights.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_STREAM_API_URL=
